BT /F2 24 Tf 48.00 793.89 Td (FounderLink Microservices End-to-End) Tj ET
BT /F2 24 Tf 48.00 763.89 Td (Workflows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 725.89 Td (Generated: May 4, 2026) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 708.89 Td (This document explains how every major user action moves from the Angular frontend, through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 694.89 Td (the API Gateway, into each Spring Boot microservice, and finally into storage,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 680.89 Td (service-to-service calls, RabbitMQ notifications, or email delivery.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.00 653.89 Td (System Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 627.89 Td (FounderLink is a full-stack microservices platform for founders, investors, co-founders, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 613.89 Td (admins. The Angular frontend uses a central AppStore to manage forms, session state,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 599.89 Td (service-page actions, and HTTP calls. The frontend talks to the backend through one gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 585.89 Td (URL: http://localhost:8080.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.00 564.89 Td (Browser user -> Angular frontend -> API Gateway -> Microservice controller -> Service layer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.00 551.89 Td (-> Repository / Feign / RabbitMQ -> Response -> Angular state update) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48.00 529.89 Td (Shared Runtime Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 510.89 Td (- User performs an action in the Angular UI.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 496.89 Td (- Angular calls a method in AppStore, such as login\(\), saveStartup\(\), createInvestment\(\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 482.89 Td (  sendInvite\(\), or sendMessage\(\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 468.89 Td (- HttpClient sends the request to http://localhost:8080.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 454.89 Td (- API Gateway routes the request by path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 440.89 Td (- Protected services validate the JWT from the Authorization header.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 426.89 Td (- The controller calls the service layer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 412.89 Td (- The service layer saves data in PostgreSQL, reads Redis cache where used, calls other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 398.89 Td (  services through Feign, or publishes notification events to RabbitMQ.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 384.89 Td (- The frontend receives the response and updates local Angular signals/state.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48.00 365.89 Td (Gateway Routes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 346.89 Td (- /auth/** -> auth-service -> port 8081) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 332.89 Td (- /users/** -> user-service -> port 8082) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 318.89 Td (- /startups/** -> startup-service -> port 8083) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 304.89 Td (- /investments/** -> investment-service -> port 8084) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 290.89 Td (- /teams/** -> team-service -> port 8085) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 276.89 Td (- /messages/** -> messaging-service -> port 8086) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 262.89 Td (- /notifications/** and /api/notifications/** -> notification-service -> port 8087) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.00 238.89 Td (API Gateway Workflow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 212.89 Td (The gateway is the single backend entry point for the frontend. It keeps the Angular app) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.00 198.89 Td (independent from individual service URLs and centralizes CORS and Swagger aggregation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 181.89 Td (- Angular builds a request URL using API_BASE, usually http://localhost:8080.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 167.89 Td (- The browser sends the request to the gateway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 153.89 Td (- Gateway matches the request path, for example /startups.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 139.89 Td (- Gateway forwards the request to the configured service URL, for example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 125.89 Td (  startup-service:8083.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 111.89 Td (- The target service returns JSON or text to the gateway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 62.00 97.89 Td (- Gateway returns the response to Angular.) Tj ET
